Work directory: <work>/find-replication (scripts named below are there). Nothing under the tree's sources, results or documents was changed; my first two runs, before I set PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, may have written the bytecode caches oracles/fresh3 .pyc into the tree's exploratory __pycache__ (other processes wrote there too).

RECOUNT (recount.py, with my own sound verdicts from sound_calc.py: 632 distinct task/program pairs re-evaluated with the reference interpreter, not the stored 'sound' lists). 207 checks, 207 matched, 0 wrong:
- stored sound lists 9/9 rows and verified counts 9/9;
- loop table 15/15 (student learning and held-out for cycles 0-3, the four teacher cells, 'two batches rejected', accepted chain, nine symbols);
- timeline fields against stored programs 33/33; the gate recomputed from programs (loop_gate.py, gate_exact.py): every accept/reject follows the family score, no rounding effect (cycle 4 batches solve exactly the same learning tasks; held-out rose to 39 in one and was not consulted);
- T, C1, C2, mid and row budgets 18/18 (T = 6 x 338 x 10^4 + 5 x 214 x 10^5 = 127,280,000; 1,126,452; 413,254; 524,267; 228,969; C1 share 36.7%);
- evaluation table 15/15; primary comparison 1/1 (71 against 64, 18 against 11, exact p = 0.13247);
- secondary bullets 28/28 (equal budgets, C2, mid, kinds 13/4/1 against 5/6 with p 0.048, strata 29-22 and 42-42, list 62-55, int/bool 9-9, clusters, leave-one-routine-out 37/37 with 62 against 63 on the 271 tasks without slice-k-n, by-symbol counts, whole pool 61-53, held-out B, combination, spent 56%-75% with spent/ceiling 18/18);
- stored comparisons 14/14; Q1-Q10 10/10 against the registered wording; class on verified counts (86 against 80, 19 against 13) also 'not established'.

PROTOCOL: outcome_class and flags_for match the registered table and the four endings branch by branch; the 'any budget' union takes exactly the registered rows (FRESH-3: 10^4, 10^5, mid, C2; held-out B: loop student0, 10^5, C1, C2); kinds read generation 0 at C2 as registered. T is an upper bound: early_stops.py shows no record above its budget in any row, and every unmatched task spends exactly its budget (no stop other than a first match; rejected batches and the final teacher run are charged; screens run no search). Arms differ only in abstractions (8 symbols), constants [10] and label (spec_diff.py); generation-0 rows carry no learned symbol in 'used'; Vocabulary.with_admitted copies. File times of replicate.py, fresh3.py, PREDICTIONS.md precede the run. MODULO in fresh3.py has 9 names against 7 registered: no FRESH-3 task has 'evens'/'odds', 104 either way. The 524,267 and 228,969 runs come after FRESH-3 rows, the 1,126,452 run first.

RESTART (restart.py): 19 loop lines of replication_interrupted.txt equal replication.json's loop (labels, budgets, learn, families, score, held-out, counts, library size, seconds, proposals, acceptances); the three finished rows have identical counts and identical spent totals; replication.json records loop_taken_from; the registration allows the restart. The interrupted process had already printed a FRESH-3 row (trained@deploy, 86 verified). I could not compare programs: the interrupted JSON is outside the allowed area.

DATA AGAINST CODE: verdicts.py re-derived every stored FRESH-3 verdict on the regenerated set (523 solved programs pass 16 examples; 446 rejected pass 8 public and fail a hidden one; no step-budget failure, no True == 1 case). tiny_repro.py (budget 2000, 2 workers) reproduced the 10^4 rows exactly where they are comparable: 87 integer/boolean tasks, 42 (generation 0) and 47 (trained) identical records, no extra or missing match; 6 + 6 list records identical.

SOUNDNESS: evidence.py: 298 of 300 FRESH-3 tasks have 200 in-domain fresh inputs, two have 19 and 46 (outputs beyond caps) and no sound solve; no task covers fewer than 2 distinct outputs; 53 of 54 boolean tasks have at least 20 inputs of the rarer answer. stress_sound.py: all 133 sound FRESH-3 programs agree on 1,713+ further in-range inputs of mine. stress_exposed.py: 214 of 214 sound learning-set programs and 68 of 69 held-out B programs pass a larger test; the one failure is a correct program that exhausts 2,000 steps on [11]x7. All not-sound verdicts on FRESH-3 are real wrong values (unsound.py). Equal-budget leads hold under audit, pool, both, verified (equal_budget_pool.py).

FRESH-3 (gen_fresh3.py, rules.py, same_function.py, program_transfer.py, hidden_pairs.py): full 64-digit digest reproduces; tally, description, 213/33/54, 8+8 distinct inputs, stage instances, no FRESH-2 routine pair, all inputs in the public pool: 0 violations. No validated reading of any exposed task (first or other) reproduces a task's 16 examples; no FRESH-3 reference agrees with an exposed reading or another FRESH-3 task on the whole pool; no program verified on a learning-set task reproduces a FRESH-3 task (two FRESH-2 programs do, both coincidental). Workers get name, type and 8 public examples; the name is used only for the record. 22 of 866 pool inputs are also hidden inputs of other FRESH tasks and trivial example pairs recur across tasks; no channel uses them.

ASYMMETRIES, disclosed, not findings: at C2 on FRESH-3 88 tasks end at a wrong first match and 26% of the ceiling stays unspent (trained at 10^5: 84 tasks, 25%); only 2 of 54 boolean tasks are solved soundly by either arm.

INTERPRETIVE SENTENCES (lead_where.py, combination.py), all supported: all 18 trained-only tasks contain slice-k-n, drop-k or a divisibility routine; on the 155 tasks without slice/take/drop/divisibility it is 32 against 37 with 0 trained-only; 62 against 63 without slice-k-n; seven first-stage routines net -1 or -2; 42 against 42 on 196; the trained state verifies the same 55 held-out B tasks as the earlier combination (sound 43 shared, 1 each).
